<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  ShokkweaveCreepWebYield.xml     ShokkweaveEconomy - new file, SHOKKWEAVE_SOLE_SOURCE_1
  ============================================================================
  The border creep-web route (owner card 4, 2026-09-11: "border creep-web
  YIELDS, with teeth" - "(2) but it has a small chance of SPAWNING an
  emergent Shokk to get you"). This item's queue line names it as the 4th
  harvest route; WEBWORK_KIT_BUILD_1 built and closed the scatter mechanism
  (RM_MapComponent_FrontCreep, live-verified 2026-09-12) but deliberately
  shipped RUT_Webwork_Anchor/_Web/_Gutter with NO killedLeavings and NO
  yield comp, leaving the attachment to this item by name (see that file's
  own "Sole-source guard" comment). This patch is that attachment - HALF of
  it; see the note at the bottom on what is still genuinely missing.

  killedLeavings, same mechanism already LIVE-VERIFIED this campaign for
  RUT_Webwork_Nest (60 Hyperweave on kill) and RUT_Webwork_SilkKnot
  (Mineable.TrySpawnYield, 4/vein): a Building's HP-to-0 destruction fires
  Destroy(DestroyMode.KillFinalize), which drops killedLeavings. Combat
  (the only destruction route these three Things have today - no
  deconstruct/harvest job exists for a natural, non-player-built Building)
  therefore already satisfies the ruling's "cutting creep-web ... yields
  Shokkweave" half.

  Counts ❓INVENTED, deliberately small: these are the per-node/per-
  line-segment pieces of a scattered network (WEBWORK_KIT_BUILD_1's own
  live test scattered 10 Anchor + 10 Web + 14 Gutter along one map edge in
  a single advance band), not a singular lair like the Nest - matching the
  spec's own "~2-5 per line-segment" range for the web-cutting route.
  Gutter (dense woven channel, highest MaxHitPoints of the three) gets the
  top of that range; Web (broad sheet, thinnest/most flammable) the bottom.

  🔴 NOT done here, and NOT safe to bolt on casually - the ruling's other
  half ("a small chance of spawning an emergent Shokk"):
  RM_CompProperties_EmergentSpawnOnDestroy (src/RimMandrake/Webwork/Source/
  RM_CompEmergentSpawnOnDestroy.cs — moved here from mandrake.rsw.shokk by
  SHOKK_SKIN_SHRINK_1, 2026-09-26, S6 ruling 1; originally built by
  SHOKK_RSW_MOD_1 as RSW_CompEmergentSpawnOnDestroy, MayRequire
  mandrake.rsw.shokk) exists and is exactly the mechanism the ruling wants -
  but its PostDestroy explicitly gates on `mode == DestroyMode.Vanish` and
  says so in its own comment: "never fires on Kill/Refund/etc." Combat
  destruction of these three Things (the ONLY destruction route they have)
  uses DestroyMode.KillFinalize, same as the Nest/SilkKnot above - so
  attaching that comp here would ship a comp that can never fire, a
  landmine that reads as "done" and isn't. The emergent-spawn half
  genuinely needs a dedicated harvest job (a WorkGiver/JobDriver/Designator
  that walks a colonist up, grants the yield, and calls
  Destroy(DestroyMode.Vanish) - the "cut" the ruling's own language implies,
  as distinct from combat-killing the node) that does not exist anywhere in
  this codebase yet. Flagging precisely rather than guessing at the job's
  shape or shipping a non-functional comp attachment.

  Wrapped in PatchOperationFindMod on the UtinniPatches mod's own display
  name: these three ThingDefs are owned by that mod (mandrake.rut.patches),
  a standing Utinni-tier co-dependency but still a SEPARATE mod from a
  patch xpath's point of view - unwrapped, a minimal/target quicktest list
  that happens to omit it would log a red config error every launch
  (validate_patch.py flagged exactly this on the unwrapped draft).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimUtinni Patches (Jawa campaign)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_Webwork_Anchor"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <killedLeavings>
          <Hyperweave>3</Hyperweave>
        </killedLeavings>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimUtinni Patches (Jawa campaign)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_Webwork_Web"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <killedLeavings>
          <Hyperweave>2</Hyperweave>
        </killedLeavings>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimUtinni Patches (Jawa campaign)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_Webwork_Gutter"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <killedLeavings>
          <Hyperweave>5</Hyperweave>
        </killedLeavings>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
